    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline already had a *hard* duplicate check (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` \u2192 409). The spec asked for a weaker *soft* match: same lastName + postcode but a different telephone should still be created, just flagged. I implemented it following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`: runs after `FlagOwnerBulkSignup`, before `SaveOwner` (so the new owner isn't compared against itself). It scans existing owners for one sharing the new owner's last name (case-insensitive) and postcode but with a *different* telephone. On a match it sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <matching id>` (lowest id when several match, for determinism); otherwise `possibleDuplicate = false` and `possibleDuplicateOf = null`. A postcode is required on both sides, so pre-existing postcode-less owners never soft-match.\n\n2. **Wired into** `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` as `flagPossibleDuplicate` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`, matching the surrounding steps).\n\n3. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with getters/setters.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the hsqldb (test), h2, mysql, and postgres `owners` tables.\n\n5. **openapi.yml** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them automatically (verified via the `GET /api/owners/{id}` assertions in the test).\n\nThe existing frozen-at-creation pattern (like `namesakeCount`/`bulkSignupWarning`) is preserved: the flags are computed once at creation and returned unchanged on later reads.",
