    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and lands exactly where a maintainer of this codebase would expect:\n\n- `FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate` mirrors its siblings (`CountOwnerNamesakes`, `FlagOwnerBulkSignup`) precisely: one public `service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)` method, a `findAll()` scan, and a derived field set on the in-place `@Val Owner`. Single, focused responsibility \u2014 not a catch-all.\n- The soft-match concept is correctly kept *separate* from the existing hard-duplicate machinery (`OwnerIdentity` / `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`). Those operate on a composite `identityKey` (telephone/email/household); the soft match is a genuinely different criterion (same lastName + postcode, *different* telephone), so folding it into `OwnerIdentity` would have muddied that abstraction. A new unit is the right call, and no matching logic is duplicated.\n- Pipeline wiring places `flagPossibleDuplicate` after `flagBulkSignup` and before `save`, with `govern: [ transaction ]` \u2014 consistent with the pre-save enrichment steps, and the Javadoc correctly justifies the ordering (runs pre-persist so the owner isn't compared against itself; runs after the hard-duplicate gate).\n- Model fields, getters/setters, all four DB schemas, and the two `readOnly` OpenAPI properties are added consistently and completely.\n\nOne minor note (not blocking): the private `equalsIgnoreCase` helper is copied verbatim from `CountOwnerNamesakes`. That duplication is already the established convention in this package (no shared string util exists), so the new class matching it is the idiomatic choice rather than a regression.",
